{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user wants me to implement a `solve(case)` function for task DATA-HDB-01 that computes a Minimum Spanning Tree using mutual reachability distances (HDBSCAN-style).\n\nLet me understand the requirements:\n1. For each pair of nodes, compute mutual reachability = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], distance(u,v))\n2. Sort edges by reachability, then by endpoint IDs (canonicalized - smaller first)\n3. Run Kruskal's algorithm with union-find to get MST\n4. Return mst_edges (list of [u, v, weight] triples) and total_weight\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    core_distance = case[\"core_distance\"]\n    distances = case[\"distances\"]\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) \u003c 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid nodes\")\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing core distance for node {node}\")\n    \n    # Compute mutual reachability for each edge\n    mr_edges = []\n    for edge in distances:\n        u, v, d = edge[0], edge[1], edge[2]\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\n        # Canonicalize: ensure u \u003c v lexicographically\n        if u \u003e v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        mr_edges.append((mr, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort by reachability then by endpoint IDs\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\n    \n    # Union-Find for Kruskal's\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]  # path compression\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    \n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\n            total_weight += mr\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\n                break\n    \n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected\")\n    \n    return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}\n```\n\nLet me verify this against the first fixture:\n\nnodes: p0, p1, p2, p3, p4\ncore_distances: p0=0.23243377, p1=0.50398147, p2=0.55673811, p3=0.66828478, p4=0.43968915\n\nDistances:\n- p0-p1: 0.89672724 → mr = max(0.23243377, 0.50398147, 0.89672724) = 0.89672724\n- p0-p2: 0.73968893 → mr = max(0.23243377, 0.55673811, 0.73968893) = 0.73968893\n- p0-p3: 0.77270596 → mr = max(0.23243377, 0.66828478, 0.77270596) = 0.77270596\n- p0-p4: 0.87376631 → mr = max(0.23243377, 0.43968915, 0.87376631) = 0.87376631\n- p1-p2: 1.08418122 → mr = max(0.50398147, 0.55673811, 1.08418122) = 1.08418122\n- p1-p3: 0.82719237 → mr = max(0.50398147, 0.66828478, 0.82719237) = 0.82719237\n- p1-p4: 0.61293041 → mr = max(0.50398147, 0.43968915, 0.61293041) = 0.61293041\n- p2-p3: 1.00286271 → mr = max(0.55673811, 0.66828478, 1.00286271) = 1.00286271\n- p2-p4: 0.5322912 → mr = max(0.55673811, 0.43968915, 0.5322912) = 0.55673811\n- p3-p4: 0.51351834 → mr = max(0.66828478, 0.43968915, 0.51351834) = 0.66828478\n\nSorted edges:\n1. p1-p4: 0.61293041\n2. p0-p2: 0.73968893\n3. p0-p3: 0.77270596\n4. p1-p3: 0.82719237\n5. p0-p4: 0.87376631\n6. p0-p1: 0.89672724\n7. p2-p3: 1.00286271\n8. p1-p2: 1.08418122\n9. p3-p4: 0.66828478 ← Wait, I need to re-sort\n\nLet me redo the sort:\n- p1-p4: 0.61293041\n- p3-p4: 0.66828478\n- p0-p2: 0.73968893\n- p0-p3: 0.77270596\n- p1-p3: 0.82719237\n- p0-p4: 0.87376631\n- p0-p1: 0.89672724\n- p2-p3: 1.00286271\n- p1-p2: 1.08418122\n- p2-p4: 0.55673811 ← This one is smallest!\n\nWait, p2-p4 mr = 0.55673811\n\nSo sorted:\n1. p2-p4: 0.55673811\n2. p1-p4: 0.61293041\n3. p3-p4: 0.66828478\n4. p0-p2: 0.73968893\n5. p0-p3: 0.77270596\n6. p1-p3: 0.82719237\n7. p0-p4: 0.87376631\n8. p0-p1: 0.89672724\n9. p2-p3: 1.00286271\n10. p1-p2: 1.08418122\n\nKruskal:\n1. p2-p4: 0.55673811 → add (components: {p0},{p1},{p2,p4},{p3})\n2. p1-p4: 0.61293041 → add, p1 joins p2,p4 (components: {p0},{p1,p2,p4},{p3})\n3. p3-p4: 0.66828478 → add, p3 joins p1,p2,p4 (components: {p0},{p1,p2,p3,p4})\n4. p0-p2: 0.73968893 → add, p0 joins all (done!)\n\nMST edges: [p2,p4,0.55673811], [p1,p4,0.61293041], [p3,p4,0.66828478], [p0,p2,0.73968893]\nTotal: 0.55673811 + 0.61293041 + 0.66828478 + 0.73968893 = 2.57764223\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me now format it as the required JSON output.\n\nThe output must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    core_distance = case[\\\"core_distance\\\"]\\n    distances = case[\\\"distances\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) \u003c 2:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid nodes list\\\")\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing core distance for node {node}\\\")\\n\\n    # Compute mutual reachability weight for each edge\\n    mr_edges = []\\n    for edge in distances:\\n        u, v, d = edge[0], edge[1], edge[2]\\n        if u not in core_distance or v not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Unknown node in distances: {u} or {v}\\\")\\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        # Canonicalize undirected endpoints: lexicographic order\\n        if u \u003e v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mr_edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n\\n    # Sort by reachability weight, then by first endpoint, then second endpoint\\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\\n\\n    # Union-Find with path compression and union by rank\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        root = x\\n        while parent[root] != root:\\n            root = parent[root]\\n        # Path compression\\n        while parent[x] != root:\\n            parent[x], x = root, parent[x]\\n        return root\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n\\n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected: cannot form a spanning tree\\\")\\n\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01k3if13vBVhpSRbGlu0i7Gi","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2387},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2387,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":66,"output_tokens":2741,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2066},"service_tier":"standard"}}